{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The sorted sets share one API: ","type":"text"},{"code":"insert(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"remove(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"contains(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"SetAlgebra","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s set","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"operations, ","type":"text"},{"code":"lowerBound(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"upperBound(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"elements(in:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and the elements as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"random-access collection in ascending order, indexed by rank. Changing which one a program uses","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a change of type name:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let avl: AVLTree = [40, 10, 30, 20]","let redBlack: RedBlackTree = [40, 10, 30, 20]","let bTree: BTree = [40, 10, 30, 20]","let skipList: SkipList = [40, 10, 30, 20]","","Array(avl)              \/\/ [10, 20, 30, 40], and the same for the others","avl.lowerBound(25)      \/\/ 2, the index of 30","bTree.lowerBound(25)    \/\/ 2"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every one takes O(log ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":") per lookup, insertion and removal (expected for the treap and skip","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"list, amortized for the splay tree). They differ in the constant, in what else they offer, and in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which workloads they suit.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Lookups and scans over a large set: BTree","type":"heading","anchor":"Lookups-and-scans-over-a-large-set-BTree"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A B-tree node (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/btrees"},{"text":") holds tens of elements side by side, so a lookup reads a few nodes and few","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cache lines, and iteration walks contiguous arrays. For a large set that is read far more often","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"than it is changed, and for range scans, a ","type":"text"},{"code":"BTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the default. Copying a B-tree shares its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nodes, and a mutated copy copies only the nodes on the path it changes. ","type":"text"},{"code":"BTreeDictionary","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its sorted dictionary.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Balanced binary trees: AVLTree and RedBlackTree","type":"heading","anchor":"Balanced-binary-trees-AVLTree-and-RedBlackTree"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"code":"AVLTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps the heights of every vertex’s subtrees within one of each other, so it is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shallowest of the binary trees and the quickest of them to search. A "},{"code":"RedBlackTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" allows a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"taller tree and in return rotates at most two or three times per insertion or removal; prefer it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when changes outnumber lookups. Both convert to a Grafluent "},{"code":"BinaryTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that shows the exact"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shape. "},{"code":"AVLDictionary","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the sorted dictionary in an AVL tree."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Splitting and joining: Treap","type":"heading","anchor":"Splitting-and-joining-Treap"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Treap"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps a random priority on each vertex, which makes its shape a random binary search"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tree’s whatever order the elements arrive in, and gives it "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"split(at:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"join(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let numbers: Treap = [8, 3, 5, 1, 9]","let parts = numbers.split(at: 5)","Array(parts.lower)            \/\/ [1, 3]","Array(parts.upper)            \/\/ [5, 8, 9]","var rejoined = parts.lower","try rejoined.join(parts.upper)","rejoined == numbers           \/\/ true"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"join(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" throws "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OverlappingKeys"},{"type":"text","text":" when the sets interleave. Pass a seeded generator to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Treap(_:using:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to make every shape reproducible. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BTree"},{"type":"text","text":" splits too."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"A working set of hot elements: SplayTree","type":"heading","anchor":"A-working-set-of-hot-elements-SplayTree"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SplayTree"},{"text":" keeps no balance information. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"access(_:)"},{"text":" and each mutation rotate the element","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"they reach to the root, so a run of lookups that keeps returning to a few elements finds them","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"near the top:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var recent: SplayTree = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]","recent.access(40)             \/\/ 40, now at the root"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Its other reads, ","type":"text"},{"code":"contains(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" among them, leave the tree as it is, so they keep value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"semantics; use ","type":"text"},{"code":"access(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" where the splay is wanted.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"A sorted queue with a simple structure: SkipList","type":"heading","anchor":"A-sorted-queue-with-a-simple-structure-SkipList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A skip list (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/skiplists","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":") stacks sorted linked levels, each holding about half the elements of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the one below. Its insertions touch only the levels an element reaches, and its levels are a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Grafluent graph through ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"layersView"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Keeping every version: PersistentTreeSet","type":"heading","anchor":"Keeping-every-version-PersistentTreeSet"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When old versions must stay readable, as in undo histories, snapshots handed to other tasks or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"backtracking searches, a persistent set ("},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/persistenttrees","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":") shares all but the vertices an edit touched:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let empty = PersistentTreeSet<Int>()","let one = empty.inserting(5)","let two = one.inserting(3)","let three = two.removing(5)","Array(one)                    \/\/ [5]","Array(two)                    \/\/ [3, 5]","Array(three)                  \/\/ [3]"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each version costs O(log "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":") new vertices rather than a copy of the whole tree."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistentTreeDictionary"},{"type":"text","text":" is the sorted dictionary."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Summary","type":"heading","anchor":"Summary"},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Workload"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Type","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Large sets, mostly lookups, range scans","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BTree"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BTreeDictionary"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mostly lookups, a binary shape to inspect"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AVLTree"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AVLDictionary"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Mostly insertions and removals","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RedBlackTree"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Splitting and joining sets"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Treap","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"BTree","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Repeated access to a few elements"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SplayTree"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every version kept","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistentTreeSet"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistentTreeDictionary"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A simple sorted queue"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"SkipList","type":"codeVoice"}]}]]]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/choosingasearchtree"]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"article","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"GrafluentCollections"}],"title":"Choosing a search tree","role":"article"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/ChoosingASearchTree"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick a sorted set or sorted dictionary by the workload it will see."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Guides","title":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/TriesAndSuffixStructures","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/DecisionDiagrams","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/RangeAndSpatialTrees","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph"],"generated":true}],"references":{"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections":{"url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"GrafluentCollections","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Graph-shaped collections for Swift: search trees, tries, suffix structures, decision diagrams,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"range and spatial trees, ropes, persistent trees and caches, with value semantics, built on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Grafluent."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections","role":"collection"},"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections/TriesAndSuffixStructures":{"url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/triesandsuffixstructures","type":"topic","title":"Tries and suffix structures","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Search a set of keys by prefix, or a text by substring.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/TriesAndSuffixStructures","role":"article"},"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections/RangeAndSpatialTrees":{"title":"Range and spatial trees","url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/rangeandspatialtrees","abstract":[{"text":"Answer queries over ranges of a sequence, over intervals, and over points in space.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/RangeAndSpatialTrees","type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/GrafluentCollections/documentation/btrees":{"title":"BTrees","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/btrees","type":"link","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/btrees","titleInlineContent":[{"code":"BTrees","type":"codeVoice"}]},"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph":{"title":"Seeing a collection as a graph","url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/seeingacollectionasagraph","abstract":[{"text":"Convert a collection’s shape to a Grafluent graph, then lay it out, write it or run an algorithm","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"over it.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph","role":"article","kind":"article"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/GrafluentCollections/documentation/persistenttrees":{"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/persistenttrees","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/persistenttrees","title":"PersistentTrees","titleInlineContent":[{"code":"PersistentTrees","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"link"},"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections/DecisionDiagrams":{"url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/decisiondiagrams","type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Decision diagrams","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Represent Boolean functions and families of sets as shared, canonical graphs."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/DecisionDiagrams","role":"article"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/GrafluentCollections/documentation/skiplists":{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/skiplists","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/skiplists","title":"SkipLists","titleInlineContent":[{"code":"SkipLists","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"link"}}}